& [Proposal]
  + carries profile ceremony UUID canonical and source identities exact runner and producer commits controller request plan and program digests exact producer-plan bytes identity executable path and digest target host ssh host ordered nineteen argument atoms timeout and stream limits one-process ceilings effect ceilings nonce decision window policy and proposal digest
  + producer plan must independently recompile from published upstream forms and the supplied executable digest; the proposal copies rather than paraphrases its exact atoms

& [Decision]
  + carries profile decision UUID ceremony UUID proposal digest operator principal role subject nonce decision authorize or reject issue time not-before expiration attempt1 permit1 process1 retry0 and a separately verifiable signature envelope identity
  + admission repeats all matched coordinates and yields admitted_authorize admitted_reject or typed_refusal; only admitted_authorize reaches permit mint

& [Permit]
  + private Rust value contains ceremony proposal decision and producer-plan identities plus attempt1 process1 and consumed false
  + no Serialize Deserialize Clone Copy Default public fields public constructor persistence or recovery form
  + consumption changes authority before any runner call and the value cannot be returned on failure

& [ReceiptAndTerminal]
  + ceremony receipt binds decision admission permit consumption runner receipt digest process accounting provider result and exactly one terminal disposition
  + terminal dispositions are completed_available completed_provider_unavailable rejected refused expired abandoned_after_consumption and receipt_refused
  + terminal record binds all predecessor digests effect account and no-retry closure

& [StrictForms]
  + canonical compact UTF-8 JSON denies duplicate unknown and trailing data with maximum bytes1048576 depth24 fields512 text8192 and exact ordered duplicate-free arrays
  + every self digest is domain-separated self-excluding SHA256 and raw bytes are retained wherever signatures or process evidence depend on byte identity
